      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">CORI3 has cystine-lyase activity based on &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; assays using purified recombinant enzyme. However, this purified enzyme does not show any transaminase/aminotransferase activity using tyrosine, aspartate, alanine, or tryptophan together with 2-oxoglutarate as a substrate |CITS: [12525491]|. CORI3 transcript levels rise in response to salt |CITS: [11351099]| and jasmonic acid applications |CITS: [11572481]|.</Comment>
